Z||000000||zero||01-15-2000||06:17 PM||||i own a 1986 2M4 with 90,000 miles.  the car runs roughly between 2000-3500 rpm's.  it runs fine cold, but after a bit of warm-up the tach momentarily 'jumps' 500-1000 rpm's, and the engine bucks.  after complete warm-up the problem is still there, but it's not as bad.  this only happens when there is a slight load on the engine.  if i step on the gas it runs smoothly again.  the dealer could not track down the problem! thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||862M4inCA||01-15-2000||06:49 PM||||Well since the dealer couldn't track any problems down, I'm assuming that if he did anything he must have checked the computer for stored codes. My only experience with a problem similar was a faulty TPS. However mine did show up trouble codes after a couple days when it was bucking on me.  If you decide to take it back to the dealer, see if he can test it.||||reg||1
